         <div type="transcription" xml:lang="pal">
            <ab xml:id="MP1029_trc-p1">
               <lb n="1" xml:id="trc-p1-l1"/>A māh Amurdād abar sāl 106 ī pas az ōy bay Yazdgird
               <lb n="2" xml:id="trc-p1-l2"/>šāhān šāh ī nab ī ōy bay Xusrō ī Ōhrmazdān ud rōz Wahman ka
               <lb n="3" xml:id="trc-p1-l3"/>Wazurgummēd ēd kē tasūg ī *dar-espāsbed ī abar Dumbāwand ī dādestān čiyōnīh
      tasūg
               <lb n="4" xml:id="trc-p1-l4"/>ham pondik wanīh ī abar Dumbāwand wisp tan must pad-iš friy būdan pad
               <lb n="5" xml:id="trc-p1-l5"/>mānīhā sōzišn ham tasūg ī pondik wanīh būd B mardān ī Bōxt nām ō 
      Wazurgummēd
               <lb n="6" xml:id="trc-p1-l6"/>guft kū mardān ī Ērāngušnasp nām Kurd pus ham tasūg ī pondik wanīh az
               <lb n="7" xml:id="trc-p1-l7"/>xwāstag sūd im rōz Wahman Ērāngušnasp xwāstag arz s(atēr) 5 sēm
               <lb n="8" xml:id="trc-p1-l8"/>dōšīh ī mardān ī Šahrdēlān nām Yazdōy pus ān ōbastag deh mānēd
               <lb n="9" xml:id="trc-p1-l9"/>az Šahrdēlān abāyēd pad kard ān xwāstag ahy wizārdan harw s(atēr) 5 gandum
               <lb n="10" xml:id="trc-p1-l10"/>g(rīw) 5 waxš ō Šahrdēlān dādan tazāg pas hamē ka Šahrdēlān gandum
               <lb n="11" xml:id="trc-p1-l11"/>xwāhēd pad pašt ī stēzag ō Šahrdēlān dādan agar tis-iz ǰuttar
               <lb n="12" xml:id="trc-p1-l12"/>kunēm tāwān-iz arz s(atēr)  3  ō  Šahrdēlān dād rāy Wahman-iz
               <lb n="13" xml:id="trc-p1-l13"/>abāg Šahrdēlān paymān kard kū en guftag ham ō tōzišn rasēd
               <lb n="14" xml:id="trc-p1-l14"/>ud paččēn ēw kunēh ō tō nē dēbahr ī man rāy ka pēšēn-tar n
               <lb n="15" xml:id="trc-p1-l15"/>Ābān ud Wahrām ud Ērāngušnasp āgenēn kard ī tis rasēd ī man pad-iz
               <lb n="16" xml:id="trc-p1-l16"/>muhr ī tō wizīr āwištan abāg tō harw pad kabīz ī tāwān wizīr bawēd
               <lb n="17" xml:id="trc-p1-l17"/>◯ ud Ērāngušnasp-iz ān Bōxt guft rāst ud Wazurgummēd ud kē nazd
               <lb n="18" xml:id="trc-p1-l18"/>mānist ◯ ud Ērāngušnasp guft kū im māh Amurdād abar sāl
               <lb n="19" xml:id="trc-p1-l19"/>106 ud rōz Wahman man xwāstag arz s(atēr) 5 sēm dōšīh ī
               <lb n="20" xml:id="trc-p1-l20"/>Šahrdēlān ān Bōxt guft az Šahrdēlān ī ham tasūg hamāg guft čiy[ō]n
               <lb n="21" xml:id="trc-p1-l21"/>Bōxt guft paymān kard ud tis-iz ī abar Bōxt guft ōwōn
               <lb n="22" xml:id="trc-p1-l22"/>did nibēsēd ud guft ān ◯ C ud ēn nāmag pad muhr ī paččēngarīh
               <lb n="23" xml:id="trc-p1-l23"/>ī Mihrīg ī ham tasūg ī *dar-espāsbed čiyōnīh ī ham tasūg ī
               <lb n="24" xml:id="trc-p1-l24"/>pondik wanīh pad must pad-iš framūd kištag framūd kištagān
               <lb n="25" xml:id="trc-p1-l25"/>ud Wazurgummēd ud Raz deh ī-š dibīr muhr ī Farroxzād
               <lb n="26" xml:id="trc-p1-l26"/>kē kard ud Ērāngušnasp āwišt ◯◯
            </ab>
         </div>
         <div type="translation" xml:lang="en">
            <ab xml:id="MP1029_trans-p1">
               <lb n="1" xml:id="trans-p1-l1"/>A month Amurdād (5th month) in the year 106 (757/8 CE) of late Lord Yazdgird,
               <lb n="2" xml:id="trans-p1-l2"/>King of Kings, grandson of the late Lord Xusrō, son of Ōhrmazd, and day Wahman (2nd day) when
               <lb n="3-4" xml:id="trans-p1-l3-4"/>Wazurgummēd who was (būd, line 5) responsible in the district of the chief of the service (of the residence) of Dumbāwand over the current (business) of the Law as well as the current (business) of everyone of the living beings (in the district of the) »Hazelnut Groves« of Dumbāwand to provide love instead of violence for
               <lb n="5" xml:id="trans-p1-l5"/>the burning of the houses in the same district of the »Hazelnut Groves« B The people of Bōxt by name to Wazurgummēd
               <lb n="6" xml:id="trans-p1-l6"/>said that the people of Ērāngušnasp by name, son of Kurd, also from the district of beyond the vineyards from the profit
               <lb n="7" xml:id="trans-p1-l7"/>of the possessions this day Wahman Ērāngušnasp a sum worth 5 staters in silver as
               <lb n="8" xml:id="trans-p1-l8"/>support for the people of Šahrdēlān by name, son of Yazdōy, who lives in the fallen village.
               <lb n="9" xml:id="trans-p1-l9"/>From Šahrdēlān it is necessary to pay the money for the affair at the soonest all 5 staters
               <lb n="10" xml:id="trans-p1-l10"/>in addition 5 grīw of wheat to be given to Šahrdēlān (and) afterwards persistently whenever Šahrdēlān asks for wheat
               <lb n="11" xml:id="trans-p1-l11"/>according to the actual agreement of the quarrel (wheat) is to be given to Šahrdēlān. If I act but a little bit otherwise
               <lb n="12" xml:id="trans-p1-l12"/>an additional compensation of 3 staters worth to be given to Šahrdēlān, Wahman together
               <lb n="13" xml:id="trans-p1-l13"/>with Šahrdēlān is to make an agreement that this which has been spoken exactly arrives at (its) rectification
               <lb n="14-15" xml:id="trans-p1-l14-15"/>and a copy is to be acquired so that you should not become angry when it will be not earlier than day Ābān (10th day) and day Wahrām (20th day) and together with Ērāngušnasp it was determined when the matter is due with your
               <lb n="16" xml:id="trans-p1-l16"/>seal, there is a decision with you on everything of the quotaNote of the recompense.
               <lb n="17" xml:id="trans-p1-l17"/>And Ērāngušnasp and that Bōxt said “right” and Wazurgummēd and those who stayed (line 18) nearby.
               <lb n="18" xml:id="trans-p1-l18"/>And Ērāngušnasp declared this month Amurdād in the year
               <lb n="19" xml:id="trans-p1-l19"/>106 and day Wahman I affirmed (line 20) money worth of 5 staters in silver as support of
               <lb n="20" xml:id="trans-p1-l20"/>Šahrdēlān that Bōxt from Šahrdēlān of the same district on the whole as
               <lb n="21" xml:id="trans-p1-l21"/>Bōxt has spoken he made an agreement even that little on which is to be spoken by Bōxt
               <lb n="22" xml:id="trans-p1-l22"/>then he should write and he said so (confirmed it). ◯ C And this document with the seal of the *copy office
               <lb n="23" xml:id="trans-p1-l23"/>of Mihrīg with the responsibility of the same district of the chief of the service (of the residence) and also of the same district of
               <lb n="24" xml:id="trans-p1-l24"/>the »Hazelnut Grove(s)«. Therefore he demanded seeds and even more seeds forcefully
               <lb n="25" xml:id="trans-p1-l25"/>and Wazurgummēd and the scribe of the Raz (wine) village (woth) the seal of Farroxzād
               <lb n="26" xml:id="trans-p1-l26"/>who made (it) and Ērāngušnasp sealed (it). 
            </ab>
         </div>
      </body>
   </text>
